# Semgrep path exclusions for the resource module scan (the repository root's
# .semgrepignore carries the same entry under its root-relative path).
#
# The property-based tests draw their cases from a seeded math/rand, which is what a
# reproducible property test needs; the crypto-randomness audit does not apply to them.
lowering_property_test.go
differential_property_test.go
semantic_differential_test.go

# The maintenance handler writes the maintenance page, embedded at compile time, to every
# navigation; no request data reaches it, so the direct-write audit (an HTML page writing
# user data) does not apply.
maintenance/maintenance.go
# The test server standing in for the Cloud Run API in the jobs package's tests answers
# JSON to the client under test; the direct-write audit (an HTML page writing user data)
# does not apply.
jobs/jobs_test.go
# The request decoder, the patch set and its diff look a struct field up by name only after
# the name has come from the resource's own type (reflect.VisibleFields, the patch set's
# keys) or from the field mapper, which refuses a JSON name the struct does not declare and
# a hidden field: no caller-chosen name reaches FieldByName, so the reflect-by-name audit
# does not apply. The generator renders Go and TypeScript source from text/template, which
# html/template's escaping would corrupt; the text-template audit does not apply.
decoder.go
patchset.go
generation/client.go
